# Rust workspace executed-test-count FLOOR.
#
# The number below is the minimum acceptable sum of passed counts across every
# `test result: ok` line of `cargo test --workspace` (unit + integration +
# doctests). CI fails if the actual executed count drops BELOW it — a test
# silently disappeared (DEFECT_CLASSES classes 7 + 10: cross-crate regression /
# platform test-gating-masks-bugs — the F18 lesson). A green crate-scoped run can
# hide a count drop; this floor is the whole-workspace catch.
#
# Protocol:
#   * Count goes UP freely. Adding tests needs no change here (CI passes whenever
#     actual >= this floor). Bumping this number up alongside a test addition is
#     encouraged so the floor stays close to reality, but not required by CI.
#   * A DROP below this floor fails CI.
#   * LOWERING this number is only legitimate when tests are deliberately removed,
#     and REQUIRES an explicit, justified commit (say why in the commit message).
#     Never lower it to make a red CI green without that justification.
#
# Provenance: 1882 measured by the leverage-pass P2 full-workspace gate
# (`cargo test --workspace`, 0 failed); P3 added documentation only (0 tests);
# P4-proptest +3 (delphi-hardening canonical_hash injectivity P1/P2/P3) -> 1885,
# verified `cargo test --workspace` 0 failed before this commit.
1885
